## Emery Platform Concepts

### Skills
AI-powered workflows that can be executed on demand or triggered automatically.
- **name**: Display name shown to users
- **description**: What the skill does (shown when selecting skills)
- **instructions**: The prompt that defines the skill's behavior when executed
- **inputs**: Array of input parameters users provide when running the skill
  - Each input has: name, type (string/number/boolean), required, description
- **outputs**: Array of output definitions describing what the skill returns
  - Each output has: name, type, description
- **tools**: Array of external integrations the skill can use (e.g., gmail_send_email, slack_send_message)
- **model**: Optional AI model override (null uses organization default)

### Tables & Data
- **Tables**: Structured data containers with typed fields (like spreadsheets)
- **Rows**: Individual records in tables
- **Fields**: Columns with types including:
  - Text, Number, Date, Boolean
  - Single Select, Multi Select
  - File, Image
  - Link (references to other tables)
- **Views**: Filtered/sorted perspectives on table data

### Agents
AI assistants configured for specific purposes.
- Can have multiple skills attached
- Have their own conversation context and memory
- Can be shared across the organization
- May have specific tools and integrations enabled

